<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cautērĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυτήσιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An instrument used for branding</i>, <i>a branding-iron</i>, <i><span class="en">Veg. 1,
				14, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 1, 28</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in medicine,</span>”
				<i>a cautery</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					25, 8, 39, § 80</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">22, 23, 49,
				§ 102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib.
				Comp. 240</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An instrument used in encaustic painting for burning
				in the wax</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 7, 17</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Herm. 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
